==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 4~8 seconds<sup>120f~240f</sup>.
**1 [[Duche]] spawns.
**1 [[Duche]] spawns.
**1 [[Duche]] spawns.
**1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
**2 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns.

==Strategy==
No strong enemies and only peons spawn before you hit the enemy base. Use [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] to stall and upgrade Worker Cat to max and wait for max money. Then, spawn all your attackers and make sure they are properly meatshielded. You might want to bring a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]] or [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] as there is a [[Metal Hippoe]], but it is not necessary as it doesn't have very high base HP.

